# CrappyFinAssist - full pipeline:
#   portfolio (Drive) -> prices/technicals -> news discovery -> sentiment -> alerts + Telegram
# Hybrid FinBERT+LLM sentiment when Ollama is reachable, FinBERT alone otherwise
# (pipeline.py decides at the start of every run).
#
# Install (appends - keeps anything already in your crontab):
#   (crontab -l 2>/dev/null; cat /home/user/ai_harness/final_cron_job) | crontab -
# Check:
#   crontab -l
# Remove:
#   crontab -l | grep -v 'ai_harness/pipeline.py' | crontab -
# Run once by hand, exactly as cron would, without sending anything:
#   cd /home/user/ai_harness && env -i HOME="$HOME" PATH=/usr/bin:/bin ./venv/bin/python3 pipeline.py --no-send
#
# Schedule - Europe/Bucharest (the system timezone), weekdays only:
#   08:00  overnight news, before any of your markets open
#   23:30  after the Frankfurt (23:00) and US (22:00-23:00, DST-dependent) closes
# Both times fall outside trading hours on purpose: yfinance's daily bars are then
# complete. A run mid-session would judge signals on a half-finished candle, and
# since the alert engine fires on *changes*, a signal flickering intraday would
# alert, clear, and alert again.
#
# What each part of the command guards against:
#   cd /home/user/ai_harness   every project path is relative (pipeline.py also chdirs itself)
#   mkdir -p logs              the redirect below needs the folder to exist
#   HARNESS_HEADLESS=1         no browser windows popping up; cron has no display anyway
#   HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1           FinBERT loads from the local cache - a Hugging Face outage can't stop a run
#   timeout --kill-after=5m 2h a hung page load / network call is killed instead of blocking later runs
#   ./venv/bin/python3         the project venv, no shell activation needed
#   >> logs/cron.log 2>&1      only catches crashes before logging starts; the real log is
#                              logs/pipeline.log (auto-rotated, 5 x 5 MB)
# Also inside pipeline.py: a lock so two runs never overlap, per-stage isolation so one
# broken phase doesn't stop the others, no interactive Drive login under cron, and a
# Telegram warning (max once per 6h) when a stage fails.

0 8 * * 1-5 cd /home/user/ai_harness && mkdir -p logs && HARNESS_HEADLESS=1 HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1 timeout --kill-after=5m 2h ./venv/bin/python3 pipeline.py >> logs/cron.log 2>&1
30 23 * * 1-5 cd /home/user/ai_harness && mkdir -p logs && HARNESS_HEADLESS=1 HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1 timeout --kill-after=5m 2h ./venv/bin/python3 pipeline.py >> logs/cron.log 2>&1
